---
title: Dumpling Tomato Salad with Chile Crisp Vinaigrette
description: Pan-fried frozen potstickers piled on a ripe tomato salad, all of it dressed in chile crisp vinaigrette.
tags: [salad]
course: main
icons: [tomato, chopsticks, salad]
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: NYT Cooking
  author: Hetty Lui McKinnon
  url: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024075-dumpling-tomato-salad-with-chile-crisp-vinaigrette
servings: 4
time: 20m
---

= Salad

Place the @ripe tomatoes{2 1/2%lb}(any variety, cut into roughly 1- to 2-inch pieces, at room temperature) on a large serving plate or in a #bowl{}. Add the @garlic clove{1}(grated), half of the @basil leaves{1/2%cup}(torn), @kosher salt{1%tsp}(such as Diamond Crystal) and a big pinch of @black pepper{}. Toss to combine and set aside.

To make the vinaigrette, combine the @chile crisp{3%tbsp}(or chile oil), @rice vinegar{2%tbsp} and @soy sauce{1%tbsp}(or more to taste) and whisk to combine. Taste and if it needs more saltiness, add 1/2 teaspoon more soy sauce.

= Dumplings

Heat a large (12-inch) nonstick or well-seasoned cast-iron #skillet{} over medium-high for ~heat{1-2%minutes} until very hot.

Add @neutral oil{1-2%tbsp}(such as canola or vegetable) and, working in batches, add the @frozen potsticker dumplings{1%lb}(not thawed), flat-side down, and cook until the bottoms of the dumplings are lightly browned, ~brown{1-2%minutes}.

Immediately add about 1/4 cup of water to the pan, just enough to cover the base of the dumplings, then cover and cook until the water has evaporated, ~steam{3-4%minutes}. (If your dumplings contain meat, cook for an extra 1 to 2 minutes, or according to packet instructions.) Transfer the cooked dumplings to a plate and continue cooking the remaining dumplings. (If you prefer to steam the dumplings, see the note below.)

To serve, place the warm dumplings over the tomato salad and drizzle with the chile crisp vinaigrette. Toss very gently. Top with the @?crispy fried shallots{1-2%tbsp}(store-bought) and the remaining basil leaves. Serve either while the dumplings are still warm or at room temperature.

> **Steaming instead** — Arrange the dumplings in a steaming basket lined with baking paper or cabbage leaves, place over a pan of boiling water and steam for 10 to 15 minutes.
